# coverage-floor ratchet — read by scripts/coverage-floor.sh (`make coverage-floor`).
#
# One line per gated package set:   <floor-pct>  <go package pattern>...
# The floor is the MINIMUM aggregate statement coverage that set may report.
# A line may only ever be RAISED (that is what a ratchet is); lowering one is a
# decision that needs a reason in the commit that does it, not a quiet edit.
#
# Seeded 2026-10-07 from the measured values below (go1.26, -short, 600s
# timeout, TestGenResolversCallsDnsvalidator skipped), each minus two points
# and rounded DOWN so a platform-specific branch cannot flake the gate:
#
#   ./internal/modules/...   measured 52.9%  (osint 51.1, subdomains 69.0,
#                                             sysinfo 66.7, vulns 41.6, web 56.3)
#   ./internal/store/...     measured 26.6%  (store/sqlc only)
#
# Raise a floor whenever a measured run clears the next whole point above it.
50 ./internal/modules/...
24 ./internal/store/...
